Now load the data into your page. Following the pattern we first covered in [Week 5](/docs/coding-the-news/scripts/week-5/), open `src/routes/+page.js` and load our JSON file into the page's properties.

```js {emphasize-lines="1,7"}
import violations from '$lib/data/bronx_buildings.json';

export function load() {
  return {
    showHeader: true,
    showFooter: true,
    violations,
  };
}
```

That will make it available in `src/routes/+page.svelte` in the `$props()` object. Open up the boilerplate page, clear it out and start over with this clean slate, which does nothing more than load the data and log it to the console:

```svelte
<script>
  let { data } = $props();

  console.log(`Loaded ${data.violations.length} buildings`);
  console.log("First record:", data.violations[0]);
</script>
```

Save the file, reload the page and open your browser's developer console. You should see the number of buildings and the first record logged out.

